So we start with S_0 = 1. Then for n ≥ 1, S_n is basically how many n by n matrices you can make where the entries are like 0,1,2,... and the matrix is symmetric (so a_ij = a_ji for all i,j) and also each column adds up to exactly 1 (so sum over i of a_ij = 1 for each j). Show that:

(a) S_{n+1} = S_n + n * S_{n-1}

(b) The exponential generating function sum from n=0 to infinity of S_n * (x^n / n!) equals exp(x + x^2/2), where exp(x) is just e^x.
